  "worked_solution": "Trigonometric functions are continuous at all points in their respective domains.\n\nThe function $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x$ is continuous over the entire interval $[-2\\pi ,0],$ but the function $\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x$ is not defined at $x=-2\\pi ,-\\pi ,0.$ \n\nTherefore, the domain of $f(x)$ consists of the union of the intervals $(-2\\pi ,-\\pi )$ and $(-\\pi ,0),$ namely\n\n$$\n(-2\\pi ,-\\pi )\\cup (-\\pi ,0)\n$$\n\nand the function is also continuous on this union of intervals.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
